//@version=6
// mVWAP-BB — the operator's VWAP setups. Script version: v37 (2026-11-13). Since v30 the number
// follows TradingView's own version counter for the operator's saved script (their save 30 = v30).
// Docs: docs/vwap-setup.md — the walkthrough, changelog, and the steps for shipping
// a new version (bump the version above, recreate the alerts).
// Four setups in one script, so the same two watchlist alerts carry them all (the VWAP +
// BB cross, the RSI cross and the EMA cross only send from the 30s alert). Each has its own "… setup on" switch: off
// = no markers and no alerts from it, and a VWAP line no setup uses isn't drawn.
// v27 removed the RECLAIM setup (FORMING / READY / GO, v1–v26) and the BB breakout
// (TOUCH / BREAKOUT / TRIGGERED, v17–v26): the operator tested all four and kept these
// two (10-28 ET). Both are in git history (v26, e38c06b) and docs/vwap-setup.md.
// 1) PULLBACK (v10): a fast run stretches price well above a VWAP line — the
// session, month or (v14) year VWAP — and it comes back down to it.
//   PULLBACK  a close back within 5% above the line after a bar high ≥15% above it → be ready
//             (v24 trial, month and year lines: the bar's low within 5% is enough, its close
//             holding at or above the line)
//   BROKEN    a close under the line → the setup is over (the operator's exit)
//   HELD      price runs +10% from the PULLBACK close first
// Each line runs its own setup, and every message carries its touch number (the
// operator rates the first pullback after the first big move highest; our own
// data found the second as good — docs/vwap-setup.md §13.5).
// 2) VWAP + BB CROSS (v21): one candle of a timeframe you pick (5m, 1h, …) crosses
// over both a VWAP line — session, and (v22) month or year — and the upper Bollinger
// Band of another timeframe you pick (45s, 2m, 30m, …). Each line runs its own setup.
//   CROSS      the candle opened under both lines (or sitting on the lower one) and a
//              30s close inside it is above both → the alert, while the candle is open
//   RETEST     (v28) after the VB candle closes, price comes back to the line it crossed
//              (within 1%) and (v30) the candle closes above it → the alert, at that close, with a
//              stop under the pullback's low (the operator's entry; v25–v27 had LEVEL / BREAK here;
//              v28–v29 fired at the first green 30s close above the line, still an option)
// Built from the 30s alert's bars; drawn on the candle's own chart.
// 3) RSI CROSS (v32): one RSI (14) crosses above its MA (SMA 14, the "RSI-based MA") while
// oversold, judged at the close of a "check" candle — the RSI's own timeframe for the plain cross
// (30m and 30m), or a shorter one (v32's default: a 12h RSI at each 6h close). Built from requests,
// so it works on the 2m chart and sends from the 30s alert; the chart marks the bar that closed the
// check candle. v33 dropped v32's second RSI (3h) and its "also require" switch.
//   RSI   the cross up while oversold, at a check candle's close
//   DIP   (v34) after an RSI cross, the RSI closes back under its MA on its own timeframe and
//         then turns up — the pullback entry, with a stop under the dip's low
// 4) EMA CROSS OVER VWAP (v35): the EMA of a timeframe's closes (3m, length 9) crosses above a
// VWAP line (session; month and year are switches), judged at each close of that timeframe's
// candles. Built from a request like the RSI, so it works on the 3m chart or a smaller one.
//   EMA   above the line at this close, at or under it at the one before
//         (v36) the filter calls a cross weak — its candle opened before 07:00 New York, the EMA
//         was under the line for fewer than 5 candles, or the two crossed more than 2 times in
//         the 20 candles before: drawn gray, sent with `| weak`, not announced
//   BOUNCE (v37) after an EMA cross, a candle's low comes down to the EMA or the VWAP and that
//         candle or a later one closes green above the EMA — the pullback entry, with a stop
//         under the pullback's low; a close under the VWAP first ends the wait
// VB lanes (v29): up to three more candle timeframes in the same alert (1h / 4h / 1D on the
// month and year lines by default), each with its own band and lines, for longer trades.
// VWAP lines (v28): from 30s bars by default, so the session line is the same on every
// chart (TradingView's built-in VWAP is built from the chart's own bars and differs by
// timeframe), or from the chart's bars ("VWAP lines from" in Inputs).
// Run it as TradingView watchlist alerts — one on 1m and one on 30s (Premium allows 2):
// Symbols = the runners list (dashboard → 📐 sidebar ⋯ → Copy list), session Extended,
// condition = this script → "Any alert() function call", once per bar close,
// webhook = https://pnldash.uz/api/tv/webhook?key=<TV_WEBHOOK_SECRET>.
// The alert message format below is parsed by apps/api/src/services/tv-setups.ts —
// keep the two in step. The offline replica (apps/api/scripts/research/vwap-setup/)
// mirrors this logic; update it with the script.
indicator("mVWAP x BB basis setup", shorttitle = "mVWAP-BB", overlay = true)

// v27 put the inputs in a new order (TradingView keeps saved values by position, so
// after the paste: Settings → Defaults → Reset settings). The defaults are the
// operator's own settings on 10-28: gainer filter 10%, VB candle 5m, band 45s.
// From here on, new inputs go last again.
// Gainer filter: computed per ticker from its own bars — no screener, no ranking.
// A ticker that doesn't pass stays silent; -100 switches the filter off.
minDayGain = input.float(10.0, "Up at least % (day high vs prior close; -100 = filter off)", group = "Gainer filter (this ticker's own move)")
runnerDays = input.int(3,      "…today, or on any of the last N sessions (0 = today only)", minval = 0, maxval = 5, group = "Gainer filter (this ticker's own move)")
useAhGain  = input.bool(true,  "After hours, also count the move since today's close", group = "Gainer filter (this ticker's own move)")
alertWin   = input.session("0400-2000", "Alert window (New York time)", group = "Alerts")
pbOn       = input.bool(true,   "Pullback setup on", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbSession  = input.bool(true,   "Lines: session VWAP", inline = "pbl", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbMonth    = input.bool(true,   "month VWAP", inline = "pbl", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbYear     = input.bool(true,   "year VWAP (v14)", inline = "pbl", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbArm      = input.float(15.0,  "Armed: a bar high at least % above the line (the big move)", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbNear     = input.float(5.0,   "PULLBACK: a close back within % above the line", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbLowMY    = input.bool(true,   "Month / year lines: a candle's low reaching the band counts, its close holding above the line (v24 trial)", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbBreak    = input.float(0.0,   "BROKEN: a close at least % under the line (0 = any close under it)", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbWin      = input.float(10.0,  "HELD: price runs % above the PULLBACK close", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbMax      = input.int(0,       "Script cap: stop a line after N failed pullbacks a day (0 = none; the dashboard applies the cap since v16)", minval = 0, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbCapMark  = input.int(2,       "Chart: pullbacks after N failed ones are drawn gray (the dashboard's cap)", minval = 1, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbTimeout  = input.int(60,      "Stop watching a pullback after N bars", minval = 1, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
vbOn       = input.bool(true,         "VWAP + BB cross setup on (v21)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbCandleTf = input.timeframe("5",     "VB: candle timeframe — the chart you trade (its candles and session VWAP)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbBbTf     = input.timeframe("45S",   "VB: BB timeframe (the band)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbLen      = input.int(20,            "VB: BB length", minval = 2, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbMult     = input.float(2.0,         "VB: BB StdDev", minval = 0.1, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbTol      = input.float(0.0,         "VB: the candle may open up to % above the lower line (price sitting on VWAP; 0 = under both)", minval = 0, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbGainOn   = input.bool(true,         "VB: gainers only (the gainer filter at the top)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbSession  = input.bool(true,         "VB lines: session VWAP", inline = "vbl", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbMonth    = input.bool(true,         "month VWAP (v22)", inline = "vbl", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbYear     = input.bool(true,         "year VWAP (v22)", inline = "vbl", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
// v28: these two kept the VB break's (v25–v27) places, so saved values stay put.
vbRtOn     = input.bool(true,         "VB retest (v28): after the VB candle closes, price back at the line it crossed and a 30s candle closing green above it", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbRtCancel = input.bool(true,         "VB retest: a candle closing back under the VWAP line the VB candle crossed cancels it", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbTf       = input.timeframe("30S",   "VB: alerts from the alert on this chart timeframe (30S = soonest)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbShow     = input.bool(true,         "VB: draw the band and markers (on the candle timeframe's chart)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
// v28 inputs go last.
vwSrc      = input.string("30s bars", "VWAP lines from (v28): 30s bars — the same line on every chart — or the chart's bars (TradingView's built-in)", options = ["30s bars", "Chart bars"], group = "Alerts")
vbRtNear   = input.float(1.0,         "VB retest: price back within % above the line (0 = to the line or under it)", minval = 0, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbRtWait   = input.int(6,             "VB retest: within N candles of the VB candle's close (0 = until cancelled)", minval = 0, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
// v29 inputs go last: three more VB timeframes ("lanes") inside the same alert, for longer trades on
// the month and year lines (operator, 10-29: "for longer terms (1h, 4h, 1D), I'd like to use VB only
// with monthly vwap (plus, yearly)"). Each lane has its own candle, band and lines; the rest (BB
// length and StdDev, tolerance, gainers, the retest, the alert timeframe) is shared with the main VB.
vb2On      = input.bool(true,         "Lane 2", inline = "vb2", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb2Cndl    = input.timeframe("60",    "candle", inline = "vb2", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb2Bb      = input.timeframe("10",    "band", inline = "vb2", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb2S       = input.bool(false,        "Lane 2 lines: session", inline = "vb2l", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb2M       = input.bool(true,         "month", inline = "vb2l", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb2Y       = input.bool(true,         "year", inline = "vb2l", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb3On      = input.bool(true,         "Lane 3", inline = "vb3", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb3Cndl    = input.timeframe("240",   "candle", inline = "vb3", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb3Bb      = input.timeframe("30",    "band", inline = "vb3", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb3S       = input.bool(false,        "Lane 3 lines: session", inline = "vb3l", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb3M       = input.bool(true,         "month", inline = "vb3l", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb3Y       = input.bool(true,         "year", inline = "vb3l", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb4On      = input.bool(true,         "Lane 4", inline = "vb4", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb4Cndl    = input.timeframe("1D",    "candle", inline = "vb4", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb4Bb      = input.timeframe("60",    "band", inline = "vb4", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb4S       = input.bool(false,        "Lane 4 lines: session", inline = "vb4l", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb4M       = input.bool(true,         "month", inline = "vb4l", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
vb4Y       = input.bool(true,         "year", inline = "vb4l", group = "VB lanes (v29)")
// v30 inputs go last.
vbRtWhen   = input.string("Candle close", "VB retest fires (v30): at the close of the candle that came back to the line, if it closes above it — or at the first green 30s close above it (v28)", options = ["Candle close", "30s bounce"], group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
rtAtClose  = vbRtWhen == "Candle close"
// v31 inputs go last.
mvSrc      = input.string("30s bars", "Month VWAP from (v31): 30s bars — this month's hourly bars + today's 30s bars, one line for every chart and setup — or the chart's bars (TradingView's anchored VWAP)", options = ["30s bars", "Chart bars"], group = "Alerts")
mv30       = mvSrc == "30s bars"

// Same lines as the chart: VWAP anchor Month on hlc3,
// and (v10, PULLBACK) VWAP anchor Session, which resets at timeframe.change("D"),
// the 04:00 ET pre-market open on an Extended chart. Each restarts on the first
// loaded bar too, exactly like TradingView's built-in VWAP
// (`if na(src[1]) … isNewPeriod := true`), so a line never goes blank when its
// anchor isn't in the loaded history (the month line late in a month on 30s).
firstBar = na(hlc3[1])
mvChart = ta.vwap(hlc3, timeframe.change("M") or firstBar)
svChart = ta.vwap(hlc3, timeframe.change("D") or firstBar)

// v28 (operator, 10-29: "vwaps in tv chart are differs for 5min and 30s"): a VWAP built
// from bars counts each bar's volume at the bar's (high + low + close) / 3, so bigger bars
// drift further from the true VWAP. On the operator's alerts since 10-23 the 5m-candle
// line sat a median 0.4% from the 30s chart's (90% within 0.9%) and the 10m one 1.6%
// (90% within 4.9%); the 1m one 0.07%. "30s bars" (the default) builds the session line,
// and today's part of the year line, from the 30s bars inside each chart bar, so every
// chart shows one line, closer to the true VWAP (and to our research's). Charts of 30s or
// less use their own bars. "Chart bars" = TradingView's built-in, as before v28. v28 left the
// month line as the chart's anchored VWAP ("most of its volume is from earlier days"); on a name
// whose one day dwarfs the month that's wrong — ROMA 10-28: the 1h chart drew ~5.94, the 30s / 1m
// alerts ~6.35, and the VB used its own line — so v31 gives the month line its own switch (below).
use30   = vwSrc == "30s bars"
chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
lower30 = use30 and chartSec > 30
need30  = (use30 or mv30) and chartSec > 30   // v31: the month line can want 30s bars on its own
[w30PV, w30V] = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, need30 ? "30S" : timeframe.period, [hlc3 * volume, volume])
float barPV = 0.0
float barV  = 0.0
int   w30N  = array.size(w30PV)
if w30N > 0
    for i = 0 to w30N - 1
        barPV := barPV + nz(array.get(w30PV, i))
        barV  := barV + nz(array.get(w30V, i))
var float s30PV = 0.0
var float s30V  = 0.0
if timeframe.change("D") or firstBar
    s30PV := 0.0
    s30V  := 0.0
s30PV := s30PV + barPV
s30V  := s30V + barV
svwap = lower30 ? (s30V > 0 ? s30PV / s30V : na) : svChart

// The year line (v11; v14 builds it from hourly bars). An intraday chart loads
// weeks of history, not a year, so a year VWAP from the chart's own bars started
// wherever the history began and differed by timeframe: SDEV 2026-10-05 was 4.36
// on the 30s chart and 4.70 on the 2m alert. v14 takes this year's 60-minute bars
// (extended hours) up to the end of yesterday, from a request that reaches back
// to January, and adds today's bars from the chart, so the 30s chart, the 1m alert
// and the 30s alert share one line. `anchorsBefore` returns the year's and (v31) the month's sums
// up to the start of the current day; they don't depend on the current hour, which is why
// lookahead_on is safe here.
anchorsBefore() =>
    var float pv     = 0.0
    var float v      = 0.0
    var float pvDay  = 0.0
    var float vDay   = 0.0
    var float mpv    = 0.0
    var float mv     = 0.0
    var float mpvDay = 0.0
    var float mvDay  = 0.0
    if timeframe.change("D")
        pvDay  := pv
        vDay   := v
        mpvDay := mpv
        mvDay  := mv
    if timeframe.change("M")
        mpv    := 0.0
        mv     := 0.0
        mpvDay := 0.0
        mvDay  := 0.0
    if timeframe.change("12M")
        pv    := 0.0
        v     := 0.0
        pvDay := 0.0
        vDay  := 0.0
    pv  := pv + hlc3 * volume
    v   := v + volume
    mpv := mpv + hlc3 * volume
    mv  := mv + volume
    [pvDay, vDay, mpvDay, mvDay]
[yPrevPV, yPrevV, mPrevPV, mPrevV] = request.security(ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker, session.extended), "60", anchorsBefore(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
var float yDayPV = 0.0
var float yDayV  = 0.0
if timeframe.change("D")
    yDayPV := 0.0
    yDayV  := 0.0
yDayPV := yDayPV + (lower30 ? barPV : hlc3 * volume)
yDayV  := yDayV + (lower30 ? barV : volume)
yvwap = na(yPrevV) or yPrevV + yDayV <= 0 ? na : (yPrevPV + yDayPV) / (yPrevV + yDayV)
// v31 "Month VWAP from: 30s bars" (the default): this month's hourly bars before today + today's
// 30s bars (the chart's own on charts of 30s or less) — the line the VB has used since v28, now also
// the one drawn and the one PULLBACK uses, the same on every chart. "Chart bars": the chart's
// anchored VWAP, as before v31 (the VB keeps its hourly-based line either way).
mvwap = mv30 ? (na(mPrevV) or mPrevV + s30V <= 0 ? na : (mPrevPV + s30PV) / (mPrevV + s30V)) : mvChart
// Strength inputs sent with every signal (v9): the signal bar's volume vs the
// average of the previous 20 bars, and the run-up over the previous 10 bars.
// PULLBACK messages carry them; the server stores them for grading.
volAvg20 = ta.sma(volume, 20)[1]
volX     = volAvg20 > 0 ? volume / volAvg20 : na
runUp10  = (close / close[10] - 1) * 100
// v21: a line is drawn while a setup that uses it is on.
plot((pbOn and pbMonth) or (vbOn and vbMonth) ? mvwap : na, "mVWAP", color.yellow)
plot((pbOn and pbSession) or (vbOn and vbSession) ? svwap : na, "sVWAP", color.purple)
plot((pbOn and pbYear) or (vbOn and vbYear) ? yvwap : na, "yVWAP", color.blue)

// Top gainer: today's high vs the prior regular-session close (like Finviz
// Change), or the same in any of the last `runnerDays` sessions — a second- or
// third-day runner sets up BEFORE it is up on the day (MEDS 2026-09-18) — or,
// after hours, the high since today's close (Finviz's AH change: AMOD fell 24%
// on 2026-10-01, then ran +70% after hours from a +19.8% day high).
newDay = timeframe.change("D")
var float lastRegClose = na
var float prevDayClose = na
var float dayHigh      = na
var dayGains = array.new<float>()   // day-high gains of finished sessions, newest first (max 5)
var float ahHigh       = na   // high since today's close (post-market bars)
if newDay
    array.unshift(dayGains, (dayHigh / prevDayClose - 1) * 100)
    if array.size(dayGains) > 5
        array.pop(dayGains)
    prevDayClose := lastRegClose
    dayHigh      := high
    ahHigh       := na
else
    dayHigh := na(dayHigh) ? high : math.max(dayHigh, high)
if session.ismarket
    lastRegClose := close
if session.ispostmarket
    ahHigh := na(ahHigh) ? high : math.max(ahHigh, high)
ahGain = session.ispostmarket and not na(ahHigh) ? (ahHigh / lastRegClose - 1) * 100 : na
dayHighGain = (dayHigh / prevDayClose - 1) * 100
float recentGain = -100.0
lookback = math.min(runnerDays, array.size(dayGains))
if lookback > 0
    for i = 0 to lookback - 1
        g = array.get(dayGains, i)
        if not na(g)
            recentGain := math.max(recentGain, g)
gainer = (not na(dayHighGain) and dayHighGain >= minDayGain) or recentGain >= minDayGain or
     (useAhGain and not na(ahGain) and ahGain >= minDayGain)

inWindow = not na(time(timeframe.period, alertWin, "America/New_York"))

pctVs(float ln) => (close >= ln ? "+" : "") + str.tostring((close / ln - 1) * 100, "#.0")

// ── 1) PULLBACK (v10) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A fast run stretches price well above a VWAP line and it comes back down to it
// (operator, 2026-10-05: SAIQ and SDEV on the session line, VEEA 2026-09-15 on
// the month line, MI 2026-10-05 12:40 ET on the year line). Each line keeps its
// own state, reset every day:
//   armed     by a bar high ≥ pbArm% above the line (gainers only)
//   PULLBACK  on a LATER close within pbNear% above the line ("be ready")
//   BROKEN    then a close pbBreak% under the line — the operator's exit — or
//   HELD      a high +pbWin% above the PULLBACK close, whichever comes first;
//             after pbTimeout bars the pullback is dropped silently.
// A close straight through the line while armed is a touch with no PULLBACK.
// Re-arming needs a new bar high ≥ pbArm% above the line. v15: the day's cap
// (pbMax) counts FAILED pullbacks — BROKEN or straight through — not every touch.
// A line that keeps holding keeps alerting (MI 2026-10-05: six year-line touches,
// every alerted one HELD, but v14's 2-touch cap blocked 11:44, 12:37 and 12:57);
// a line that failed twice stops. Four months of session-line data: at least as good
// on every exit rule, ~2 more alerts a day (docs/vwap-setup.md §13.5).
// v16 (2026-10-10): the cap moved to the dashboard. The script alerts every
// pullback (pbMax 0) and each PULLBACK says how many failed before it on its line
// (`fails N`); the server stays quiet past 2 failures unless the ticker is on our
// Momentum list at grade B+ or better (WFF 10-09: a year-line pullback ran +40%
// past the cap). Cap tweaks no longer need a new script or new alerts.
type PbLine
    bool  armed    = false
    int   armBar   = na
    float peakPct  = na
    int   touches  = 0
    int   fails    = 0
    bool  open     = false
    float entry    = na
    int   alertBar = na

// One bar of one line's setup: 0 nothing, 1 PULLBACK, 2 BROKEN, 3 HELD.
// v24 (operator, RBNE 10-21 04:10 ET: the dip tagged the month line's band with its
// low, ~1.20 over a ~1.17 line, but closed 7–8% above it, then ran to 1.92): `useLow`
// lets the bar's low reach the band, the close still at or above the line. A trial on
// the month and year lines only — on four months of the session line (research/
// vwap-pullback --touch low) the low added ~2 alerts a day at 0.3–0.9 points worse a
// trade, and the month and year lines can only be graded live. Such a PULLBACK's
// message shows its close more than pbNear % above the line.
method step(PbLine s, float ln, bool canArm, bool useLow) =>
    int ev = 0
    if not na(ln) and ln > 0
        if s.open
            if close < ln * (1 - pbBreak / 100)
                s.open  := false
                s.fails := s.fails + 1
                ev := 2
            else if high >= s.entry * (1 + pbWin / 100)
                s.open := false
                ev := 3
            else if bar_index - s.alertBar >= pbTimeout
                s.open := false
        if not s.open
            float stretch = (high / ln - 1) * 100
            if not s.armed
                if canArm and stretch >= pbArm
                    s.armed   := true
                    s.armBar  := bar_index
                    s.peakPct := stretch
            else
                s.peakPct := math.max(s.peakPct, stretch)
                float reach = useLow ? low : close
                if bar_index > s.armBar and reach <= ln * (1 + pbNear / 100)
                    s.armed   := false
                    s.touches := s.touches + 1
                    if close < ln * (1 - pbBreak / 100)
                        s.fails := s.fails + 1
                    else if ev == 0 and (pbMax == 0 or s.fails < pbMax)
                        s.open     := true
                        s.entry    := close
                        s.alertBar := bar_index
                        ev := 1
    ev

var PbLine pbS = PbLine.new()
var PbLine pbM = PbLine.new()
var PbLine pbY = PbLine.new()
if newDay
    pbS.armed   := false
    pbS.open    := false
    pbS.touches := 0
    pbS.fails   := 0
    pbM.armed   := false
    pbM.open    := false
    pbM.touches := 0
    pbM.fails   := 0
    pbY.armed   := false
    pbY.open    := false
    pbY.touches := 0
    pbY.fails   := 0
int evS = 0
int evM = 0
int evY = 0
if pbOn and inWindow
    if pbSession
        evS := pbS.step(svwap, gainer, false)
    if pbMonth
        evM := pbM.step(mvwap, gainer, pbLowMY)
    if pbYear
        evY := pbY.step(yvwap, gainer, pbLowMY)

// The message — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage:
//   PULLBACK SAIQ 6.2 | sVWAP 6.16 (+0.7%) | mVWAP 4.1 (+51.2%) | line session | touch 2 | fails 0 | peak +17% | day high +336% | vol 0.6x | run -9.6% | tf 1
// v16: `fails` = failed pullbacks on the line before this one (the lowest of the lines named).
pbMsg(int ev, string lineName, int touch, float peak, int fails) =>
    string msg = (ev == 1 ? "PULLBACK" : ev == 2 ? "BROKEN" : "HELD") + " " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(svwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(svwap) + "%)"
    msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(mvwap) + "%)"
    if not na(yvwap)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(yvwap) + "%)"
    msg += " | line " + lineName + " | touch " + str.tostring(touch)
    if ev == 1
        msg += " | fails " + str.tostring(fails)
    if ev == 1 and not na(peak)
        msg += " | peak +" + str.tostring(peak, "#") + "%"
    msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(volX)
        msg += " | vol " + str.tostring(volX, "#.#") + "x"
    if not na(runUp10)
        msg += " | run " + (runUp10 >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(runUp10, "#.#") + "%"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period

// Lines firing the same event on one bar (they sit close together early in a
// month) are one message naming all of them, e.g. "line session+month" (v10–v13
// said "both" for session + month): the lowest touch number and failure count, the highest peak.
pbJoin(string acc, string name) => acc == "" ? name : acc + "+" + name
pbFire(int e) =>
    string names = ""
    int touch = 999
    int fails = 999
    float peak = na
    if evS == e
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
        touch := math.min(touch, pbS.touches)
        fails := math.min(fails, pbS.fails)
        peak  := na(peak) ? pbS.peakPct : math.max(peak, nz(pbS.peakPct, peak))
    if evM == e
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
        touch := math.min(touch, pbM.touches)
        fails := math.min(fails, pbM.fails)
        peak  := na(peak) ? pbM.peakPct : math.max(peak, nz(pbM.peakPct, peak))
    if evY == e
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
        touch := math.min(touch, pbY.touches)
        fails := math.min(fails, pbY.fails)
        peak  := na(peak) ? pbY.peakPct : math.max(peak, nz(pbY.peakPct, peak))
    [names, touch, peak, fails]

[pbN1, pbT1, pbP1, pbF1] = pbFire(1)
[pbN2, pbT2, pbP2, pbF2] = pbFire(2)
[pbN3, pbT3, pbP3, pbF3] = pbFire(3)
if pbN1 != ""
    alert(pbMsg(1, pbN1, pbT1, pbP1, pbF1), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if pbN2 != ""
    alert(pbMsg(2, pbN2, pbT2, pbP2, pbF2), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if pbN3 != ""
    alert(pbMsg(3, pbN3, pbT3, pbP3, pbF3), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// v16: a pullback past the dashboard's cap (pbCapMark failures on every line it names)
// is drawn gray — it only pings for a B+-or-better ticker on our Momentum list.
bool pbCapped = pbN1 != "" and pbF1 >= pbCapMark
plotshape(pbN1 != "" and not pbCapped, "Pullback", shape.diamond, location.belowbar, color.aqua, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(pbCapped, "Pullback (past the cap)", shape.diamond, location.belowbar, color.gray, size = size.tiny)
// v28: BROKEN and HELD are hidden by default (the operator hides them); Style can show them.
plotshape(evS == 2 or evM == 2 or evY == 2, "Broken", shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.red, size = size.tiny, display = display.none)
plotshape(evS == 3 or evM == 3 or evY == 3, "Held", shape.flag, location.abovebar, color.lime, size = size.tiny, display = display.none)

// ── 2) VWAP + BB CROSS (v21; v22 adds the month and year lines) ───────────────
// The operator's fourth setup (2026-10-20; AIXI, WORX and NWGL on 5m charts): "the
// market is colder than before, and it's very hard to trade with 1min timeframe".
// On a chart of their choice (5m, 1h, …) with its session VWAP and the upper
// Bollinger Band of another timeframe (2m on the 5m chart; 30m or 45m on the 1h
// chart), one candle crosses over both lines. They want the alert at that moment,
// not at the candle's close. v22 (operator: "it's ok to add a support for month and
// year"): the same rule on the month and the year VWAP, each line with its own state.
//   CROSS  at a 30s close inside the candle, its open is at or under both the line and
//          the band as they stand then (at most vbTol % over the lower one: price
//          sitting on the line counts) and the close is above both → the alert; once
//          per candle and line. v23 (operator, WHLR 10-21 04:00 ET: "this one
//          definitely should be considered as a VB … if 1 candle crosses both vwap and
//          bb upper row"): the lines as they stand at that close — what the chart
//          draws for the candle — not as they stood when it opened, and the day's
//          first candle counts. A 04:00 gap-and-go (WHLR 0.36 → open 0.43 → 0.55)
//          drags its own VWAP and band above its open; v21/v22 saw an open above
//          yesterday's lines and stayed silent.
// Premium's two watchlist-alert slots are taken (1m + 30s), so it rides the 30s alert
// (like v17–v26's breakout): vbStep() builds the candle, its VWAP lines and the band (SMA /
// StdDev of the BB timeframe's closes, the forming one live) from the 30s bars. The
// session line is the candle timeframe's own (hlc3 × volume of its candles). A 30s
// chart doesn't hold a month of history, so the month and year lines take the days
// before today from this year's hourly bars (vbAnchors(), like the year line since
// v14) and add today's candles. The candle's chart replays the same 30s bars
// (request.security_lower_tf), so its markers are the alerts. Gainers only by
// default: the filter at the top, recomputed from the 30s bars
// (a request can't read the chart's running values). Lines firing on one 30s bar are
// one message (`line session+month`); `cross N` counts the day's crosses on each line
// (the lowest of the lines named), and the server announces the first few
// (TV_SETUP.vb_cap).
vbOk  = vbOn and timeframe.in_seconds(vbCandleTf) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf) and timeframe.in_seconds(vbBbTf) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf)
// v29: the lanes, on with the main switch.
vb2Ok = vbOn and vb2On and timeframe.in_seconds(vb2Cndl) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf) and timeframe.in_seconds(vb2Bb) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf)
vb3Ok = vbOn and vb3On and timeframe.in_seconds(vb3Cndl) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf) and timeframe.in_seconds(vb3Bb) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf)
vb4Ok = vbOn and vb4On and timeframe.in_seconds(vb4Cndl) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf) and timeframe.in_seconds(vb4Bb) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf)

// The month's and the year's Σ hlc3 × volume and Σ volume up to the start of the
// current day, on hourly bars (extended hours). They don't depend on the current
// hour, which is why lookahead_on is safe here (as in anchorsBefore()).
vbAnchors() =>
    var float aMPV  = 0.0
    var float aMV   = 0.0
    var float aYPV  = 0.0
    var float aYV   = 0.0
    var float aMPVd = 0.0
    var float aMVd  = 0.0
    var float aYPVd = 0.0
    var float aYVd  = 0.0
    bool aNewDay   = timeframe.change("D")
    bool aNewMonth = timeframe.change("M")
    bool aNewYear  = timeframe.change("12M")
    if aNewDay
        aMPVd := aMPV
        aMVd  := aMV
        aYPVd := aYPV
        aYVd  := aYV
    if aNewMonth
        aMPV  := 0.0
        aMV   := 0.0
        aMPVd := 0.0
        aMVd  := 0.0
    if aNewYear
        aYPV  := 0.0
        aYV   := 0.0
        aYPVd := 0.0
        aYVd  := 0.0
    aMPV := aMPV + hlc3 * volume
    aMV  := aMV + volume
    aYPV := aYPV + hlc3 * volume
    aYV  := aYV + volume
    [aMPVd, aMVd, aYPVd, aYVd]

// One line's CROSS test, on the line and the band as they stand now (v23): the candle's
// open is at or under the higher of them and at most vbTol % over the lower one, and
// the close is above both — the candle's body crosses both.
vbCan(float ln, float up, float cOpen, bool fired) =>
    not fired and not na(ln) and not na(up) and cOpen <= math.max(ln, up) and cOpen <= math.min(ln, up) * (1 + vbTol / 100) and close > ln and close > up

// v26: the lowest of the VWAP lines a VB candle crossed (session / month / year), na if none is known.
vbLowest(bool onS, bool onM, bool onY, float lnS, float lnM, float lnY) =>
    float lowLn = na
    if onS and not na(lnS)
        lowLn := lnS
    if onM and not na(lnM)
        lowLn := na(lowLn) ? lnM : math.min(lowLn, lnM)
    if onY and not na(lnY)
        lowLn := na(lowLn) ? lnY : math.min(lowLn, lnY)
    lowLn

// v28: the highest of them — the first line a pullback reaches, the one the retest watches.
vbHighest(bool onS, bool onM, bool onY, float lnS, float lnM, float lnY) =>
    float hiLn = na
    if onS and not na(lnS)
        hiLn := lnS
    if onM and not na(lnM)
        hiLn := na(hiLn) ? lnM : math.max(hiLn, lnM)
    if onY and not na(lnY)
        hiLn := na(hiLn) ? lnY : math.max(hiLn, lnY)
    hiLn

// v29: one call per lane (its own state): the candle and band timeframes, its lines, and whether
// it is on (and valid against the alert timeframe).
vbStep(simple string cTf, simple string bTf, bool onS, bool onM, bool onY, bool laneOk) =>
    // Called on every bar: and/or are lazy in v6, so the timeframe tests and the
    // request come first.
    bool gNewDay   = timeframe.change("D")
    bool vNewBb    = timeframe.change(bTf)
    bool vNewCndl  = timeframe.change(cTf)
    bool vCarry    = timeframe.in_seconds(cTf) >= 14400   // v29: 4h+ candles carry a month / year retest overnight
    bool vEndsNow  = time_close == time_close(cTf)        // v30: this bar closes the candle
    bool vInWin    = not na(time(timeframe.period, alertWin, "America/New_York"))
    [vMBPV, vMBV, vYBPV, vYBV] = request.security(ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker, session.extended), "60", vbAnchors(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
    // The gainer filter, as at the top of the script.
    var float gLastReg = na
    var float gPrev    = na
    var float gHigh    = na
    var float gAhHigh  = na
    var gGains = array.new<float>()   // finished sessions' day-high gains, newest first (max 5)
    if gNewDay
        array.unshift(gGains, (gHigh / gPrev - 1) * 100)
        if array.size(gGains) > 5
            array.pop(gGains)
        gPrev   := gLastReg
        gHigh   := high
        gAhHigh := na
    else
        gHigh := na(gHigh) ? high : math.max(gHigh, high)
    if session.ismarket
        gLastReg := close
    if session.ispostmarket
        gAhHigh := na(gAhHigh) ? high : math.max(gAhHigh, high)
    float gAh     = session.ispostmarket and not na(gAhHigh) ? (gAhHigh / gLastReg - 1) * 100 : na
    float gDay    = (gHigh / gPrev - 1) * 100
    float gRecent = -100.0
    int   gLook   = math.min(runnerDays, array.size(gGains))
    if gLook > 0
        for i = 0 to gLook - 1
            float gOne = array.get(gGains, i)
            if not na(gOne)
                gRecent := math.max(gRecent, gOne)
    bool gOk = (not na(gDay) and gDay >= minDayGain) or gRecent >= minDayGain or (useAhGain and not na(gAh) and gAh >= minDayGain)
    // The band: the BB timeframe's last vbLen - 1 finished closes plus the forming one.
    var vCloses = array.new<float>()
    var float vLastC = na
    if vNewBb and not na(vLastC)
        array.push(vCloses, vLastC)
        if array.size(vCloses) > vbLen - 1
            array.shift(vCloses)
    vLastC := close
    float vBand = na
    int   vN    = array.size(vCloses)
    if vN == vbLen - 1
        float vSum = close
        for i = 0 to vN - 1
            vSum := vSum + array.get(vCloses, i)
        float vMean = vSum / vbLen
        float vSq   = math.pow(close - vMean, 2)
        for i = 0 to vN - 1
            vSq := vSq + math.pow(array.get(vCloses, i) - vMean, 2)
        vBand := vMean + vbMult * math.sqrt(vSq / vbLen)
    // The candle, and the day's Σ over its finished candles.
    var float vPV      = 0.0     // Σ hlc3 × volume…
    var float vV       = 0.0     // …and Σ volume
    var float vOpen    = na
    var float vHigh    = na
    var float vLow     = na
    var float vClose   = na
    var float vVol     = 0.0
    var bool  vSFired  = false
    var bool  vMFired  = false
    var bool  vYFired  = false
    var int   vSCount  = 0
    var int   vMCount  = 0
    var int   vYCount  = 0
    var vVols = array.new<float>()   // the last 20 finished candles' volumes
    // v28: the latest VB candle's retest — the lines it crossed, whether price has come back to
    // the line yet, the pullback's low, and the candles since the VB candle closed.
    var bool  vRtS     = false
    var bool  vRtM     = false
    var bool  vRtY     = false
    var bool  vRtArmed = false
    var bool  vRtTouch = false
    var float vRtLow   = na
    var int   vRtAge   = 0
    var int   vRtCount = 0
    var float vPrevVw  = na     // v26: the last bar's lines (where they stood at the candle's close)
    var float vPrevMw  = na
    var float vPrevYw  = na
    var float vPV30    = 0.0    // v28: today's Σ hlc3 × volume and Σ volume over the 30s bars
    var float vV30     = 0.0
    var bool  vEndSeen = false  // v30: the forming candle's closing bar has been judged
    bool  vRt     = false
    bool  vRtLate = false       // v31: judged on the next candle's first bar (its closing bar had no trades)
    float vRtStop = na
    float vRtPx   = na          // v30: the RETEST's price — the candle's close (with "Candle close")
    if gNewDay or vNewCndl or na(vOpen)
        // v30: a candle whose closing 30s bar had no trades is judged here, on its last bar's values
        // (30 s late); normally the candle's own closing bar judges it (below).
        if rtAtClose and vRtArmed and vRtTouch and not vEndSeen and not na(vOpen)
            float vLnE = vbHighest(vRtS, vRtM, vRtY, vPrevVw, vPrevMw, vPrevYw)
            if not na(vLnE) and vClose > vLnE and vInWin
                vRtArmed := false
                vRt      := true
                vRtStop  := vRtLow - syminfo.mintick
                vRtPx    := vClose
                vRtLate  := true
                vRtCount := vRtCount + 1
        vEndSeen := false
        // The candle that just closed (its values are still here): a VB candle arms a retest,
        // replacing the last one. A new day clears it — except (v29) on a lane of 4h or longer
        // candles, where a retest of the month / year lines carries over (a 4h candle closing at
        // 20:00, a daily one); one involving the session line still ends with the session.
        if gNewDay
            vRtCount := 0
            if vRtArmed and (vRtS or not vCarry)
                vRtArmed := false
        if vbRtOn and not na(vOpen) and (vSFired or vMFired or vYFired) and not (gNewDay and (vSFired or not vCarry))
            vRtS     := vSFired
            vRtM     := vMFired
            vRtY     := vYFired
            vRtArmed := true
            vRtTouch := false
            vRtLow   := na
            vRtAge   := 0
        else if vRtArmed and not na(vOpen)
            vRtAge := vRtAge + 1
        // v26: that candle — the VB candle itself or a later one — closed under the lowest line the
        // VB candle crossed: the retest is off. So is one past vbRtWait candles.
        if vbRtCancel and vRtArmed and not na(vOpen)
            float vLnC = vbLowest(vRtS, vRtM, vRtY, vPrevVw, vPrevMw, vPrevYw)
            if not na(vLnC) and vClose < vLnC
                vRtArmed := false
        if vRtArmed and vbRtWait > 0 and vRtAge >= vbRtWait
            vRtArmed := false
        if not na(vOpen)
            array.push(vVols, vVol)
            if array.size(vVols) > 20
                array.shift(vVols)
        if gNewDay
            vPV     := 0.0
            vV      := 0.0
            vSCount := 0
            vMCount := 0
            vYCount := 0
        else if not na(vOpen)
            vPV := vPV + (vHigh + vLow + vClose) / 3 * vVol
            vV  := vV + vVol
        vOpen    := open
        vHigh    := high
        vLow     := low
        vVol     := volume
        vSFired  := false
        vMFired  := false
        vYFired  := false
    else
        vHigh := math.max(vHigh, high)
        vLow  := math.min(vLow, low)
        vVol  := vVol + volume
    vClose := close
    if gNewDay
        vPV30 := 0.0
        vV30  := 0.0
    vPV30 := vPV30 + hlc3 * volume
    vV30  := vV30 + volume
    // Today's part of the lines: the candles' (hlc3 × volume of each candle, the forming one
    // included — the candle chart's built-in VWAP) or, with "30s bars" (v28), the 30s bars'.
    float vTPV    = use30 ? vPV30 : vPV + (vHigh + vLow + close) / 3 * vVol
    float vTV     = use30 ? vV30 : vV + vVol
    float vVw     = vTV > 0 ? vTPV / vTV : na
    float vMPV    = mv30 ? vPV30 : vTPV    // v31: the month line's today, per its own switch
    float vMV     = mv30 ? vV30 : vTV
    float vMw     = not na(vMBV) and vMBV + vMV > 0 ? (vMBPV + vMPV) / (vMBV + vMV) : na
    float vYw     = not na(vYBV) and vYBV + vTV > 0 ? (vYBPV + vTPV) / (vYBV + vTV) : na
    float vAvgVol = array.size(vVols) > 0 ? array.avg(vVols) : na
    float vVolX   = not na(vAvgVol) and vAvgVol > 0 ? vVol / vAvgVol : na
    bool  vOkAll  = laneOk and vInWin and (not vbGainOn or gOk)
    bool  vFireS  = vOkAll and onS and vbCan(vVw, vBand, vOpen, vSFired)
    bool  vFireM  = vOkAll and onM and vbCan(vMw, vBand, vOpen, vMFired)
    bool  vFireY  = vOkAll and onY and vbCan(vYw, vBand, vOpen, vYFired)
    if vFireS
        vSFired := true
        vSCount := vSCount + 1
    if vFireM
        vMFired := true
        vMCount := vMCount + 1
    if vFireY
        vYFired := true
        vYCount := vYCount + 1
    // v28 RETEST (the operator's entry): from the first bar after the VB candle closed, a bar whose
    // low comes within vbRtNear % above the highest line the VB candle crossed (or under it), then
    // the first bar from there that closes above that line and above its own open — the bounce.
    // The stop is a tick under the pullback's low (the lowest low since the VB candle closed).
    // Measured (research/vwap-bb-cross/vb_retest_study.py, 5m candles, 06-12 → 10-28): −0.92% a
    // trade against −1.26% for the v25 break and −1.87% for the CROSS, a 2.2% median stop, 22%
    // reaching 2R first; per unit of risk the break did better (−0.14R vs −0.30R). A heads-up.
    // v30 (operator, CLPT 10-29: "RT should not be fired if its candle's close is under the vwap"):
    // with "Candle close" (the default) the RETEST waits for the close of the candle that came back to
    // the line and fires only if that candle closes above it; a close under the lowest crossed line
    // cancels it (above). Measured (vb_retest_study.py, 5m / 10m, 06-12 → 10-28): −0.84% / −0.83% a
    // trade vs −0.92% / −0.91% at the 30s bounce, −0.26R / −0.18R vs −0.31R / −0.25R (stops ≥ 0.5%),
    // stopped 57% vs 63%; also requiring a green candle was worse (−1.44% / −1.21%).
    float vRtLine = vbHighest(vRtS, vRtM, vRtY, vVw, vMw, vYw)
    if vRtArmed
        vRtLow := na(vRtLow) ? low : math.min(vRtLow, low)
        if not vRtTouch and not na(vRtLine) and low <= vRtLine * (1 + vbRtNear / 100)
            vRtTouch := true
        bool vRtGo = rtAtClose ? vEndsNow and close > vRtLine : close > vRtLine and close > open
        if vRtTouch and vInWin and not na(vRtLine) and vRtGo
            vRtArmed := false
            vRt      := true
            vRtStop  := vRtLow - syminfo.mintick
            vRtPx    := close
            vRtCount := vRtCount + 1
    if vEndsNow
        vEndSeen := true
    vPrevVw := vVw
    vPrevMw := vMw
    vPrevYw := vYw
    [vFireS, vFireM, vFireY, vVw, vMw, vYw, vBand, vOpen, gDay, gAh, vVolX, vSCount, vMCount, vYCount, vRt, vRtStop, vRtS, vRtM, vRtY, vRtCount, vRtPx, vRtLate]

// On the alert's own chart (30s): the alert, and its markers there (the main VB's).
[vbFireS, vbFireM, vbFireY, vbVw, vbMw, vbYw, vbBand, vbOpen, vbDayG, vbAhG, vbVolX, vbNS, vbNM, vbNY, vbRt, vbRtStop, vbRtS, vbRtM, vbRtY, vbRtN, vbRtPx, vbRtLate] = vbStep(vbCandleTf, vbBbTf, vbSession, vbMonth, vbYear, vbOk)
// v29: the lanes, each its own state.
[v2FireS, v2FireM, v2FireY, v2Vw, v2Mw, v2Yw, v2Band, v2Open, v2DayG, v2AhG, v2VolX, v2NS, v2NM, v2NY, v2Rt, v2RtStop, v2RtS, v2RtM, v2RtY, v2RtN, v2RtPx, v2RtLate] = vbStep(vb2Cndl, vb2Bb, vb2S, vb2M, vb2Y, vb2Ok)
[v3FireS, v3FireM, v3FireY, v3Vw, v3Mw, v3Yw, v3Band, v3Open, v3DayG, v3AhG, v3VolX, v3NS, v3NM, v3NY, v3Rt, v3RtStop, v3RtS, v3RtM, v3RtY, v3RtN, v3RtPx, v3RtLate] = vbStep(vb3Cndl, vb3Bb, vb3S, vb3M, vb3Y, vb3Ok)
[v4FireS, v4FireM, v4FireY, v4Vw, v4Mw, v4Yw, v4Band, v4Open, v4DayG, v4AhG, v4VolX, v4NS, v4NM, v4NY, v4Rt, v4RtStop, v4RtS, v4RtM, v4RtY, v4RtN, v4RtPx, v4RtLate] = vbStep(vb4Cndl, vb4Bb, vb4S, vb4M, vb4Y, vb4Ok)
// On a candle timeframe's chart: the same 30s bars inside each candle, for the lane whose candle
// timeframe the chart is (the main VB first) — one replay, whichever chart it is.
// v30: the choice reads timeframe.main_period, the chart's timeframe even inside the replay's request.
// v29 read timeframe.period, which inside request.security_lower_tf is the requested 30S, so a
// lane's chart (CLPT 1h, 10-29) replayed the main 5m VB — its session crosses and retests — instead.
vlN    = timeframe.main_period == vbCandleTf ? 1 : vb2On and timeframe.main_period == vb2Cndl ? 2 : vb3On and timeframe.main_period == vb3Cndl ? 3 : vb4On and timeframe.main_period == vb4Cndl ? 4 : 1
vlCndl = vlN == 2 ? vb2Cndl : vlN == 3 ? vb3Cndl : vlN == 4 ? vb4Cndl : vbCandleTf
vlBb   = vlN == 2 ? vb2Bb : vlN == 3 ? vb3Bb : vlN == 4 ? vb4Bb : vbBbTf
vlS    = vlN == 2 ? vb2S : vlN == 3 ? vb3S : vlN == 4 ? vb4S : vbSession
vlM    = vlN == 2 ? vb2M : vlN == 3 ? vb3M : vlN == 4 ? vb4M : vbMonth
vlY    = vlN == 2 ? vb2Y : vlN == 3 ? vb3Y : vlN == 4 ? vb4Y : vbYear
vlOk   = vlN == 2 ? vb2Ok : vlN == 3 ? vb3Ok : vlN == 4 ? vb4Ok : vbOk
vbView() =>
    [vwS, vwM, vwY, vwVw, vwMw, vwYw, vwBand, vwOpen, vwDayG, vwAhG, vwVolX, vwNS, vwNM, vwNY, vwRt, vwRtStop, vwRtS, vwRtM, vwRtY, vwRtN, vwRtPx, vwRtLate] = vbStep(vlCndl, vlBb, vlS, vlM, vlY, vlOk)
    [vwS, vwM, vwY, vwBand, vwRt and not vwRtLate, vwRt and vwRtLate]
vbBaseSec  = timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf)
vbChartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
vbLower    = vlOk and vbShow and timeframe.period == vlCndl and vbChartSec > vbBaseSec
[vbInS, vbInM, vbInY, vbInUp, vbInRt, vbInRtL] = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, vbLower ? vbTf : timeframe.period, vbView())
bool  vbMarkS = false
bool  vbMarkM = false
bool  vbMarkY = false
bool  vbMarkR = false
bool  vbMarkRL = false   // v31: a late RETEST, drawn on the candle before (the one that closed above the line)
float vbUp    = na
if vbLower
    int vbIn = array.size(vbInS)
    if vbIn > 0
        vbUp := array.get(vbInUp, vbIn - 1)   // the band at the candle's last 30s close
        for k = 0 to vbIn - 1
            if array.get(vbInS, k)
                vbMarkS := true
            if array.get(vbInM, k)
                vbMarkM := true
            if array.get(vbInY, k)
                vbMarkY := true
            if array.get(vbInRt, k)
                vbMarkR := true
            if array.get(vbInRtL, k)
                vbMarkRL := true
else if vbOk and vbShow and vbChartSec == vbBaseSec
    vbMarkS := vbFireS
    vbMarkM := vbFireM
    vbMarkY := vbFireY
    vbMarkR  := vbRt and not vbRtLate
    vbMarkRL := vbRt and vbRtLate
    vbUp     := vbBand

// The message — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage. The VWAPs are
// the setup's lines (the candle timeframe's session VWAP, the hourly-anchored month
// and year VWAPs), upper the BB timeframe's band, open the candle's:
//   CROSS AIXI 2.61 | sVWAP 2.47 (+5.7%) | mVWAP 2.55 (+2.4%) | yVWAP 3.1 (-15.8%) | upper 2.58 (+1.2%) | open 2.5 | line session+month | candle 5 | bb 2 | cross 1 | day high +25% | vol 1.8x | tf 30S
vbSend  = vbOk and timeframe.period == vbTf
vb2Send = vb2Ok and timeframe.period == vbTf
vb3Send = vb3Ok and timeframe.period == vbTf
vb4Send = vb4Ok and timeframe.period == vbTf
// v29: one message builder for every lane (the lane's own values passed in).
vbMsg(bool lFS, bool lFM, bool lFY, int lNS, int lNM, int lNY, float lVw, float lMw, float lYw, float lBand, float lOpen, float lDayG, float lAhG, float lVolX, string lCTf, string lBTf) =>
    string names = ""
    int    n     = 999
    if lFS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
        n     := math.min(n, lNS)
    if lFM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
        n     := math.min(n, lNM)
    if lFY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
        n     := math.min(n, lNY)
    string msg = "CROSS " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    if not na(lVw)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(lVw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lVw) + "%)"
    if not na(lMw)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(lMw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lMw) + "%)"
    if not na(lYw)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(lYw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lYw) + "%)"
    msg += " | upper " + str.tostring(lBand, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lBand) + "%)"
    msg += " | open " + str.tostring(lOpen, format.mintick)
    msg += " | line " + names + " | candle " + lCTf + " | bb " + lBTf + " | cross " + str.tostring(n)
    if not na(lDayG)
        msg += " | day high " + (lDayG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lDayG, "#") + "%"
    if not na(lAhG)
        msg += " | ah " + (lAhG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lAhG, "#") + "%"
    if not na(lVolX)
        msg += " | vol " + str.tostring(lVolX, "#.#") + "x"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period

if vbSend and (vbFireS or vbFireM or vbFireY)
    alert(vbMsg(vbFireS, vbFireM, vbFireY, vbNS, vbNM, vbNY, vbVw, vbMw, vbYw, vbBand, vbOpen, vbDayG, vbAhG, vbVolX, vbCandleTf, vbBbTf), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if vb2Send and (v2FireS or v2FireM or v2FireY)
    alert(vbMsg(v2FireS, v2FireM, v2FireY, v2NS, v2NM, v2NY, v2Vw, v2Mw, v2Yw, v2Band, v2Open, v2DayG, v2AhG, v2VolX, vb2Cndl, vb2Bb), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if vb3Send and (v3FireS or v3FireM or v3FireY)
    alert(vbMsg(v3FireS, v3FireM, v3FireY, v3NS, v3NM, v3NY, v3Vw, v3Mw, v3Yw, v3Band, v3Open, v3DayG, v3AhG, v3VolX, vb3Cndl, vb3Bb), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if vb4Send and (v4FireS or v4FireM or v4FireY)
    alert(vbMsg(v4FireS, v4FireM, v4FireY, v4NS, v4NM, v4NY, v4Vw, v4Mw, v4Yw, v4Band, v4Open, v4DayG, v4AhG, v4VolX, vb4Cndl, vb4Bb), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// v28 RETEST (operator, AIOK 10-28/29: "I'm not using BREAKs for enter (because they can be very
// extended by the moment entering), but waiting 1st 5min candle closes with VB and pulls back to
// vwap line and bounces, I'm entering right at that moment"). It replaces v25–v27's LEVEL / BREAK;
// `retest N` counts the day's retests on the ticker (per lane since v29), and the server caps them.
//   RETEST AIOK 17.28 | stop 17.09 | sVWAP 17.1 (+1.1%) | mVWAP 14.2 (+21.7%) | line session | candle 5 | bb 45S | retest 1 | day high +46% | vwap 30s | tf 30S
vbRtMsg(bool lRS, bool lRM, bool lRY, float lStop, float lVw, float lMw, float lYw, int lRN, float lDayG, float lAhG, string lCTf, string lBTf, float lPx) =>
    string names = ""
    if lRS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
    if lRM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
    if lRY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
    string msg = "RETEST " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(na(lPx) ? close : lPx, format.mintick)
    msg += " | stop " + str.tostring(lStop, format.mintick)
    if not na(lVw)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(lVw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lVw) + "%)"
    if not na(lMw)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(lMw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lMw) + "%)"
    if not na(lYw)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(lYw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lYw) + "%)"
    msg += " | line " + names + " | candle " + lCTf + " | bb " + lBTf + " | retest " + str.tostring(lRN)
    if not na(lDayG)
        msg += " | day high " + (lDayG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lDayG, "#") + "%"
    if not na(lAhG)
        msg += " | ah " + (lAhG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lAhG, "#") + "%"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period

if vbSend and vbRt
    alert(vbRtMsg(vbRtS, vbRtM, vbRtY, vbRtStop, vbVw, vbMw, vbYw, vbRtN, vbDayG, vbAhG, vbCandleTf, vbBbTf, vbRtPx), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if vb2Send and v2Rt
    alert(vbRtMsg(v2RtS, v2RtM, v2RtY, v2RtStop, v2Vw, v2Mw, v2Yw, v2RtN, v2DayG, v2AhG, vb2Cndl, vb2Bb, v2RtPx), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if vb3Send and v3Rt
    alert(vbRtMsg(v3RtS, v3RtM, v3RtY, v3RtStop, v3Vw, v3Mw, v3Yw, v3RtN, v3DayG, v3AhG, vb3Cndl, vb3Bb, v3RtPx), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if vb4Send and v4Rt
    alert(vbRtMsg(v4RtS, v4RtM, v4RtY, v4RtStop, v4Vw, v4Mw, v4Yw, v4RtN, v4DayG, v4AhG, vb4Cndl, vb4Bb, v4RtPx), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
plot(vbShow and (vbLower or (vbOk and vbChartSec == vbBaseSec)) ? vbUp : na, "BB upper (VWAP + BB cross)", color.new(color.orange, 20))
// v22: the marker says which line crossed (the year's, then the month's, first): teal
// for the session line, yellow "VB M" for the month line, blue "VB Y" for the year line.
plotshape(vbMarkS and not vbMarkM and not vbMarkY, "VWAP + BB cross (session)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.teal, text = "VB", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(vbMarkM and not vbMarkY, "VWAP + BB cross (month, v22)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.yellow, text = "VB M", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
plotshape(vbMarkY, "VWAP + BB cross (year, v22)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.blue, text = "VB Y", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(vbMarkR, "VB retest (v28)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.lime, text = "RT", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
// v31: a RETEST judged on the next bar (its candle's closing 30s bar had no trades) is drawn on that
// candle, one bar back — ROMA 1h 10-28 drew one on the candle after. Its own plot (last in the list);
// give it the same style as "VB retest (v28)" in Style if you restyled that one.
plotshape(vbMarkRL, "VB retest, late close (v31)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.lime, text = "RT", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small, offset = -1)

// ── 3) RSI CROSS (v32) and its DIP (v34) ──────────────────────────────────────
// Operator, 2026-11-08 (XTND and DKI on a 6h chart with two RSIs, 12h and 3h): "12h rsi must be
// oversold; signal is, when 12h rsi crosses the smoothing line" — for longer trades, without
// leaving the 2m chart. The RSI is TradingView's (ta.rma of the gains and losses, as the default
// RSI script) and its MA the default "RSI-based MA" (SMA 14). A request returns the RSI's state
// after its last finished candle (lookahead on + [1]: no repainting); the live value at this bar
// comes from that state and the bar's close, as the RSI's own chart shows it. It is sampled when a
// check candle closes ("RSI: checked at the close of"): a signal is the RSI above its MA at that
// close after being at or under it at the previous one, with the RSI at or under the oversold
// level then or within its last N candles (DKI 10-03: crossed at ~31 after ~22 a few candles
// earlier). No gainer filter: these are beaten-down names. A candle whose closing bar had no
// trades is judged on the next bar and drawn one bar back (as v31's late RT).
// v33 (operator, 11-10: "The experiment with 2 different RSIs failed … remove the second rsi (keep
// only one) and remove its checkbox"): one RSI. Checked on the replica (pinesim.selftest_rsi, and
// five names' 2m bars over 60 days): a 30m RSI checked at the 30m close marks the plain rule's
// crosses on a 30m, 2m or 1m chart.
// v34 DIP (operator, 11-12, OMH, a 15m RSI checked at the 1h close: "can we add a signal when RSI
// cross signal fires and rsi purple line crosses down the smoothing line (and find the deepest part
// of it somehow)"). After an RSI cross the script follows the RSI at each close of its own
// timeframe's candles:
//   the dip starts  the RSI closes under its MA, within "RSI dip: it must start within N" candles
//   DIP             the first candle that closes with the RSI higher than the candle before, after
//                   the dip's lowest RSI so far — the low was one candle ago; a lower low and
//                   another rise gives the next DIP (at most "RSI dip: at most N signals"). If the
//                   RSI gets back over its MA without one, that close is the DIP.
//   the dip is over when the RSI closes back over its MA; the next RSI cross arms the next one.
// The message carries a stop a tick under the dip's lowest price. Untested on our data.
// v34 also: a candle left unsampled is sampled before the bar's own closes (v33's else-if skipped
// it when one bar ended both), and the marks are drawn only on charts whose bars line up with the
// candles sampled (v33 drew wrong ones on the 1h / 4h charts): a chart no bigger than the RSI's
// timeframe that divides the check timeframe; the DIP marks need a chart that divides the RSI's
// timeframe too (a 15m RSI: 15m, 5m, 3m, 1m — not 10m).
// v32 inputs go last.
rsOn    = input.bool(true,       "RSI setup on (v32): the RSI crosses above its MA while oversold — marks on charts up to the RSI's timeframe", group = "RSI cross (v32)")
rsCheck = input.timeframe("360", "RSI: checked at the close of these candles (6h; the RSI's own timeframe = the plain cross)", group = "RSI cross (v32)")
rsTfA   = input.timeframe("720", "RSI: the RSI's timeframe (12h)", group = "RSI cross (v32)")
rsLen   = input.int(14,          "RSI: length", minval = 2, group = "RSI cross (v32)")
rsMaLen = input.int(14,          "RSI: MA length (SMA — TradingView's “RSI-based MA”)", minval = 2, group = "RSI cross (v32)")
rsOs    = input.float(30.0,      "RSI: oversold — the RSI at or under this…", group = "RSI cross (v32)")
rsOsN   = input.int(6,           "…at the cross or within its last N candles (0 = at the cross)", minval = 0, group = "RSI cross (v32)")
// v34 inputs go last.
rsDipOn   = input.bool(true,     "RSI dip (v34): after an RSI cross, the RSI closes back under its MA and then turns up — the pullback entry", group = "RSI cross (v32)")
rsDipWait = input.int(16,        "RSI dip: it must start within N of the RSI's candles after the RSI cross (0 = until the next RSI cross)", minval = 0, group = "RSI cross (v32)")
rsDipMax  = input.int(2,         "RSI dip: at most N signals per dip (each after a new lower RSI low)", minval = 1, group = "RSI cross (v32)")

// The RSI timeframe's state after its last finished candle: close, the two rma's, the sum of the
// last (MA length − 1) RSI values, and the lowest RSI of the last N candles.
rsState(simple int len, simple int maLen, simple int lowN) =>
    float ch = ta.change(close)
    float up = ta.rma(math.max(ch, 0), len)
    float dn = ta.rma(-math.min(ch, 0), len)
    float r  = dn == 0 ? 100.0 : up == 0 ? 0.0 : 100.0 - 100.0 / (1.0 + up / dn)
    float sm = math.sum(r, maLen - 1)
    float lo = ta.lowest(r, math.max(lowN, 1))
    [close[1], up[1], dn[1], sm[1], lo[1]]
rsSym = ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker, session.extended)
[rsCA, rsUA, rsDA, rsSmA, rsLoA] = request.security(rsSym, rsTfA, rsState(rsLen, rsMaLen, rsOsN), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
// The RSI and its MA as that timeframe's chart shows them now: the finished candles + `px` as the open one's close.
rsLive(float c0, float up, float dn, float sm, float px) =>
    float ch = px - c0
    float u  = (up * (rsLen - 1) + math.max(ch, 0)) / rsLen
    float d  = (dn * (rsLen - 1) + math.max(-ch, 0)) / rsLen
    float r  = d == 0 ? 100.0 : u == 0 ? 0.0 : 100.0 - 100.0 / (1.0 + u / d)
    [r, (sm + r) / rsMaLen]
[rsA, rsMaA] = rsLive(rsCA, rsUA, rsDA, rsSmA, close)
float rsLowA = rsOsN > 0 ? math.min(nz(rsLoA, rsA), rsA) : rsA

// The setup's state, stepped once per sampled candle close (no history inside: a bar can sample two).
type RsiSetup
    float prevA  = na      // the cross: the RSI and its MA at the previous check close
    float prevMa = na
    float prevR  = na      // the dip: the RSI at the previous close of its own candles
    bool  armed  = false   // an RSI cross fired: watching for the dip
    int   age    = 0       // the RSI's candles since that cross
    bool  inDip  = false   // the RSI has closed under its MA
    float lowR   = na      // the dip's lowest RSI…
    bool  lowNew = false   // …made by the last candle (a rise now is the turn)
    float lowPx  = na      // the dip's lowest price
    int   n      = 0       // DIP signals sent in this dip

// A check candle's close → true on a cross up while oversold.
method checkCross(RsiSetup s, float r, float ma, float lo) =>
    bool up = not na(s.prevA) and not na(r) and s.prevA <= s.prevMa and r > ma and lo <= rsOs
    if not na(r)
        s.prevA  := r
        s.prevMa := ma
    up

// An RSI cross fired: watch for its dip.
method armDip(RsiSetup s) =>
    s.armed  := true
    s.age    := 0
    s.inDip  := false
    s.lowR   := na
    s.lowNew := false
    s.lowPx  := na
    s.n      := 0
    true

// A close of the RSI's own candle (`cLow` = that candle's low) → 0 nothing, 1 the dip starts, 2 DIP.
method stepDip(RsiSetup s, float r, float ma, float cLow) =>
    int ev = 0
    if not na(r) and not na(ma)
        if s.armed
            s.age := s.age + 1
            if not s.inDip
                if r < ma
                    s.inDip  := true
                    s.lowR   := r
                    s.lowNew := true
                    s.lowPx  := cLow
                    s.n      := 0
                    ev := 1
                else if rsDipWait > 0 and s.age >= rsDipWait
                    s.armed := false
            else
                s.lowPx := na(s.lowPx) ? cLow : math.min(s.lowPx, cLow)
                bool rose = not na(s.prevR) and r > s.prevR
                if ((rose and s.lowNew) or (r > ma and s.n == 0)) and s.n < rsDipMax
                    s.n := s.n + 1
                    ev := 2
                if r > ma
                    s.armed := false
                    s.inDip := false
                else if r < s.lowR
                    s.lowR   := r
                    s.lowNew := true
                else
                    s.lowNew := false
        s.prevR := r
    ev

// Where the samples are right: the chart's bars must line up with the candles sampled.
rsChartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
rsCheckSec = timeframe.in_seconds(rsCheck)
rsTfSec    = timeframe.in_seconds(rsTfA)
rsCrossOk  = rsOn and rsChartSec <= rsTfSec and rsCheckSec % rsChartSec == 0
rsDipOk    = rsCrossOk and rsDipOn and rsTfSec % rsChartSec == 0

// A candle is sampled on the bar that closes it, or (its closing bar had no trades) late, on the
// next bar, from the bar before. One bar can do both: the late ones first.
rsT     = time(rsCheck)
rsTA    = time(rsTfA)
rsEndC  = time_close == time_close(rsCheck)
rsEndA  = time_close == time_close(rsTfA)
var int rsDoneC = na
var int rsDoneA = na
bool rsLateC = not na(rsT[1]) and rsT != rsT[1] and (na(rsDoneC) or rsDoneC != rsT[1])
bool rsLateA = not na(rsTA[1]) and rsTA != rsTA[1] and (na(rsDoneA) or rsDoneA != rsTA[1])
// The low of the RSI's candle so far, and of the one before (for a late sample).
var float rsCLow  = na
var float rsCLowP = na
if na(rsTA[1]) or rsTA != rsTA[1]
    rsCLowP := rsCLow
    rsCLow  := low
else
    rsCLow := math.min(rsCLow, low)

var RsiSetup rs = RsiSetup.new()
bool  rsFire  = false
bool  rsLate  = false
float rsSA    = na
float rsSMa   = na
float rsSLo   = na
float rsSPx   = na
bool  rsDipFrom = false   // the dip started on this bar's sample
bool  rsDipGo   = false
bool  rsDipLate = false
float rsDR    = na
float rsDMa   = na
float rsDLo   = na        // the dip's lowest RSI
float rsDPx   = na
float rsDStop = na
int   rsDN    = 0
int   rsDAge  = 0
if rsCrossOk
    // Candles that ended before this bar, unsampled: the dip's, then the cross's.
    if rsDipOk and rsLateA
        int rsE1 = rs.stepDip(rsA[1], rsMaA[1], rsCLowP)
        rsDoneA := rsTA[1]
        if rsE1 == 1
            rsDipFrom := true
        if rsE1 == 2
            rsDipGo   := true
            rsDipLate := true
            rsDR      := rsA[1]
            rsDMa     := rsMaA[1]
            rsDPx     := close[1]
            rsDLo     := rs.lowR
            rsDStop   := rs.lowPx - syminfo.mintick
            rsDN      := rs.n
            rsDAge    := rs.age
    if rsLateC
        bool rsF1 = rs.checkCross(rsA[1], rsMaA[1], rsLowA[1])
        rsDoneC := rsT[1]
        if rsF1
            rsFire := true
            rsLate := true
            rsSA   := rsA[1]
            rsSMa  := rsMaA[1]
            rsSLo  := rsLowA[1]
            rsSPx  := close[1]
            rs.armDip()
    // The candles this bar closes.
    if rsDipOk and rsEndA and (na(rsDoneA) or rsDoneA != rsTA)
        int rsE2 = rs.stepDip(rsA, rsMaA, rsCLow)
        rsDoneA := rsTA
        if rsE2 == 1
            rsDipFrom := true
        if rsE2 == 2
            rsDipGo   := true
            rsDipLate := false
            rsDR      := rsA
            rsDMa     := rsMaA
            rsDPx     := close
            rsDLo     := rs.lowR
            rsDStop   := rs.lowPx - syminfo.mintick
            rsDN      := rs.n
            rsDAge    := rs.age
    if rsEndC and (na(rsDoneC) or rsDoneC != rsT)
        bool rsF2 = rs.checkCross(rsA, rsMaA, rsLowA)
        rsDoneC := rsT
        if rsF2
            rsFire := true
            rsLate := false
            rsSA   := rsA
            rsSMa  := rsMaA
            rsSLo  := rsLowA
            rsSPx  := close
            rs.armDip()
// Announced inside the alert window only (the state above runs on).
rsFire  := rsFire and inWindow
rsDipGo := rsDipGo and inWindow

// The messages — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage (v32 also sent a second
// "| rsi 180 … ma …", which the server still reads on old rows):
//   RSI XTND 1.07 | rsi 30 29.2 ma 27.0 | low 22.1 | candle 30 | tf 30S
//   DIP OMH 8.02 | rsi 15 31.5 ma 32.8 | low 30.4 | stop 7.88 | dip 1 | since 6 | candle 15 | tf 30S
// (DIP: `low` the dip's lowest RSI, `stop` a tick under its lowest price, `dip` the signal's number
// in this dip, `since` the RSI's candles since the RSI cross, `candle` the RSI's timeframe.)
rsMsg() =>
    string msg = "RSI " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(rsSPx, format.mintick)
    msg += " | rsi " + rsTfA + " " + str.tostring(rsSA, "#.0") + " ma " + str.tostring(rsSMa, "#.0")
    msg += " | low " + str.tostring(rsSLo, "#.0") + " | candle " + rsCheck
    if rsLate
        msg += " | late"
    msg + " | tf " + timeframe.period
rsDipMsg() =>
    string msg = "DIP " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(rsDPx, format.mintick)
    msg += " | rsi " + rsTfA + " " + str.tostring(rsDR, "#.0") + " ma " + str.tostring(rsDMa, "#.0")
    msg += " | low " + str.tostring(rsDLo, "#.0") + " | stop " + str.tostring(rsDStop, format.mintick)
    msg += " | dip " + str.tostring(rsDN) + " | since " + str.tostring(rsDAge) + " | candle " + rsTfA
    if rsDipLate
        msg += " | late"
    msg + " | tf " + timeframe.period

// From the 30s alert alone (the VB's alert timeframe), like the VB.
if rsFire and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(rsMsg(), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if rsDipGo and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(rsDipMsg(), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
plotshape(rsFire and not rsLate, "RSI cross (v32)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.purple, text = "RSI", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(rsFire and rsLate, "RSI cross, late close (v32)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.purple, text = "RSI", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, offset = -1)
// v34 plots go last: the DIP, and a small mark where the dip started (the RSI closed under its MA).
plotshape(rsDipGo and not rsDipLate, "RSI dip (v34)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.fuchsia, text = "DIP", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(rsDipGo and rsDipLate, "RSI dip, late close (v34)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.fuchsia, text = "DIP", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, offset = -1)
plotshape(rsDipFrom, "RSI dip starts (v34)", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.purple, size = size.tiny)

// ── 4) EMA CROSS OVER VWAP (v35) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Operator, 2026-11-13: "I want to be notified when ema crosses up the vwap (for example, 9 ema
// crosses up the session vwap in 3 min chart timeframe)". The EMA of a timeframe's closes against
// a VWAP line, judged at each close of that timeframe's candles: above the line now, at or under
// it at the close before. As the RSI: a request returns the EMA after the last finished candle
// (lookahead on + [1]) and the bar's close makes it live, so it works on any chart whose bars
// divide the timeframe and sends from the 30s alert. The lines are the script's own (the session
// line from 30s bars by default), the ones it draws.
// A candle whose closing bar had no trades is judged on the next bar (`| late`), except across the
// day's end: yesterday's last candle is not announced this morning (the 11-10 audit: such RETESTs
// arrived hours late). A line's first candle after its anchor restarts (the session line's first
// of the day) can't fire: the "cross" there is the line starting over.
// Gainers only by default; `cross N` counts the day's crosses sent on the line, and the server
// announces the first few on Momentum names (TV_SETUP.em_cap), like the VB.
// v35 inputs go last.
emOn      = input.bool(true,     "EMA cross setup on (v35): an EMA crosses above a VWAP line, judged at a candle's close", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emTf      = input.timeframe("3", "EMA: candle timeframe (the EMA of its closes; judged at each close)", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emLen     = input.int(9,         "EMA: length", minval = 1, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emSession = input.bool(true,     "EMA lines: session VWAP", inline = "eml", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emMonth   = input.bool(false,    "month VWAP", inline = "eml", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emYear    = input.bool(false,    "year VWAP", inline = "eml", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emGainOn  = input.bool(true,     "EMA: gainers only (the gainer filter at the top)", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emShow    = input.bool(true,     "EMA: draw the EMA line and the markers", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
// v36 inputs go last: the filter (operator, 11-13, PARA: "is there anyway we can filter/optimize the
// false ones?"). Measured on our data (research/ema-vwap, 08-14 → 11-13, 3,768 crosses): about half
// close back under the VWAP within 5 candles, and three things mark the worse ones in both halves of
// the data — the hour (before 07:00 ET: 60–64% false), a short stay under the line before the cross
// (under 5 candles: 56–62%) and crossing back and forth before it (5+ flips in 20 candles: 64%). The
// crosses this filter calls weak were false 57% of the time, the rest 41–44%; the plain cross loses
// either way (a heads-up, not an edge), and the ADX and volume filters of the video did nothing.
// A weak cross is drawn gray and its message says `| weak`: the server stores it and stays quiet.
emFilterOn = input.bool(true,    "EMA filter on (v36): weak crosses are drawn gray and sent quietly", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emMinUnder = input.int(5,        "EMA filter: the EMA was under the line for at least N candles before the cross", minval = 0, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emMaxFlips = input.int(2,        "EMA filter: at most N EMA / line crossings in the 20 candles before", minval = 0, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emFromHour = input.int(7,        "EMA filter: not before this hour, New York time (4 = from the pre-market open)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
// v37 inputs go last: the BOUNCE (operator, 11-13, PARA with v36's marks: "maybe, pullback or bounce
// from ema and/or vwap can help?"). Measured first (research/ema-vwap/ema_pullback_study.py, the same
// 3,768 crosses): waiting after a cross for a candle whose low comes down to the EMA or the VWAP and
// then a green close above the EMA takes about 44% of the crosses. Those entries close back under the
// VWAP within 5 candles 35% of the time (the cross itself: 48%) and lose about −0.08R with a stop
// under the pullback's low and a 2R target (the cross: −0.21R) — in both halves of the data, on 5m
// candles, and with a 5 or a 20 candle wait. The crosses that never give one are mostly the failures
// (65–70% false), not runs that got away. Fewer false ones and under half the loss; still not an edge.
// A bounce after a weak cross is weak too: gray, `| weak`, not announced.
emBncOn   = input.bool(true,           "EMA bounce on (v37): after an EMA cross, a pullback to the EMA or the VWAP, then a green close above the EMA", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncFrom = input.string("EMA or VWAP", "EMA bounce: the pullback comes down to", options = ["EMA or VWAP", "EMA", "VWAP"], group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncWait = input.int(10,              "EMA bounce: within N candles after the cross", minval = 1, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncTolE = input.float(0.0,           "EMA bounce: a low within this % above the EMA counts as a touch", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncTolV = input.float(1.0,           "EMA bounce: a low within this % above the VWAP counts as a touch", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncE = emBncFrom != "VWAP"
emBncV = emBncFrom != "EMA"

// The EMA after the last finished candle of its timeframe, and live at this bar (that EMA's
// chart value now: the finished candles + this bar's close as the open one's).
emPrevE = request.security(rsSym, emTf, ta.ema(close, emLen)[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
emAlpha = 2.0 / (emLen + 1)
emLive  = emAlpha * close + (1 - emAlpha) * emPrevE
// Where the samples are right: a chart no bigger than the EMA's timeframe whose bars divide it.
emTfSec = timeframe.in_seconds(emTf)
emOk    = emOn and rsChartSec <= emTfSec and emTfSec % rsChartSec == 0

// One line's state, stepped once per sampled candle close.
type EmaLine
    float prevE = na    // the EMA and the line at the candle close before
    float prevL = na
    int   n     = 0     // the day's crosses sent on this line (v36: the weak ones aren't counted)
    int   under = 0     // v36: closes in a row with the EMA at or under the line, up to the last one
    int   ran   = 0     // v36: at the last cross, how many closes the EMA had been under the line…
    int   flips = 0     // …and how many times the two had crossed in the 20 closes before it
    bool  armed = false // v37: a cross is waiting for its bounce
    int   age   = 0     // candles since that cross's candle
    bool  hitE  = false // a candle's low has come down to the EMA since…
    bool  hitV  = false // …or to the line
    float lowP  = na    // the lowest low since that touch (the stop goes a tick under it)
    bool  weakX = false // the cross was weak (v36), so its bounce is
    int   bn    = 0     // the day's bounces sent on this line (the weak ones aren't counted)

// A candle close → true when the EMA crossed above the line. `hist` is this line's last 20 closes
// (1 = the EMA above the line), kept beside the object.
method crossUp(EmaLine s, array<int> hist, float e, float ln) =>
    bool up = not na(s.prevE) and not na(e) and not na(ln) and s.prevE <= s.prevL and e > ln
    if not na(e) and not na(ln)
        if up
            s.ran := s.under
            int f = 0
            int m = array.size(hist)
            if m > 1
                for i = 1 to m - 1
                    if array.get(hist, i) != array.get(hist, i - 1)
                        f += 1
            s.flips := f
        s.under := e > ln ? 0 : s.under + 1
        array.push(hist, e > ln ? 1 : 0)
        if array.size(hist) > 20
            array.shift(hist)
        s.prevE := e
        s.prevL := ln
    up

// The line's anchor restarted: its next candle has no close before it.
method restart(EmaLine s, array<int> hist) =>
    s.prevE := na
    s.prevL := na
    s.under := 0
    s.armed := false
    array.clear(hist)
    true

// v37: a sent cross starts the wait for its bounce (a newer cross starts it over).
method arm(EmaLine s, bool weak) =>
    s.armed := true
    s.age   := 0
    s.hitE  := false
    s.hitV  := false
    s.lowP  := na
    s.weakX := weak
    true

// v37: one candle close of the wait → true at the bounce. The candle's low comes down to the EMA or
// the line (a touch; from then on the lowest low is kept), and the same candle or a later one closes
// green above the EMA. A close under the line first, or emBncWait candles without one, ends the wait.
method stepBounce(EmaLine s, float e, float ln, float cOpen, float cLow, float cClose) =>
    bool go = false
    if s.armed and not na(e) and not na(ln) and not na(cOpen) and not na(cLow)
        s.age := s.age + 1
        if emBncE and cLow <= e * (1 + emBncTolE / 100)
            s.hitE := true
        if emBncV and cLow <= ln * (1 + emBncTolV / 100)
            s.hitV := true
        if s.hitE or s.hitV
            s.lowP := na(s.lowP) ? cLow : math.min(s.lowP, cLow)
        if cClose < ln
            s.armed := false
        else if (s.hitE or s.hitV) and cClose > cOpen and cClose > e
            go := true
            s.armed := false
        else if s.age >= emBncWait
            s.armed := false
    go

// v36: a weak cross — too early in the day, too short a stay under the line, or too much crossing before it.
emWeak(EmaLine s, bool early) => emFilterOn and (early or s.ran < emMinUnder or s.flips > emMaxFlips)

// The fired lines' best reading, for the message: the longest stay under the line and the fewest flips.
emRead(EmaLine s, EmaLine m, EmaLine y, bool fS, bool fM, bool fY) =>
    int u = 0
    int f = 999
    if fS
        u := math.max(u, s.ran)
        f := math.min(f, s.flips)
    if fM
        u := math.max(u, m.ran)
        f := math.min(f, m.flips)
    if fY
        u := math.max(u, y.ran)
        f := math.min(f, y.flips)
    [u, f]

// The lowest of the fired lines' counts (as the VB's `cross N`).
emCount(EmaLine s, EmaLine m, EmaLine y, bool fS, bool fM, bool fY) =>
    int n = 999
    if fS
        n := math.min(n, s.n)
    if fM
        n := math.min(n, m.n)
    if fY
        n := math.min(n, y.n)
    n

// v37: the fired lines' bounce, for the message — the lowest pullback low, the fewest candles since
// the cross, what the pullback came down to, and the lowest of the day's counts.
emBRead(EmaLine s, EmaLine m, EmaLine y, bool fS, bool fM, bool fY) =>
    float lo = na
    int   ag = 999
    bool  hE = false
    bool  hV = false
    int   n  = 999
    if fS
        lo := s.lowP
        ag := s.age
        hE := s.hitE
        hV := s.hitV
        n  := s.bn
    if fM
        lo := na(lo) ? m.lowP : math.min(lo, m.lowP)
        ag := math.min(ag, m.age)
        hE := hE or m.hitE
        hV := hV or m.hitV
        n  := math.min(n, m.bn)
    if fY
        lo := na(lo) ? y.lowP : math.min(lo, y.lowP)
        ag := math.min(ag, y.age)
        hE := hE or y.hitE
        hV := hV or y.hitV
        n  := math.min(n, y.bn)
    [lo, ag, hE, hV, n]

var EmaLine emS = EmaLine.new()
var EmaLine emM = EmaLine.new()
var EmaLine emY = EmaLine.new()
var emHS = array.new<int>()   // v36: each line's last 20 closes (1 = the EMA above it), for the flips
var emHM = array.new<int>()
var emHY = array.new<int>()
emT   = time(emTf)
emEnd = time_close == time_close(emTf)
var int emDone = na
bool emLateS = not na(emT[1]) and emT != emT[1] and (na(emDone) or emDone != emT[1])
bool emNewM  = timeframe.change("M")
bool emNewY  = timeframe.change("12M")
// v37: the open and the low of the EMA's candle so far, and of the one before (for a late sample).
var float emCO  = na
var float emCL  = na
var float emCOp = na
var float emCLp = na
if na(emT[1]) or emT != emT[1]
    emCOp := emCO
    emCLp := emCL
    emCO  := open
    emCL  := low
else
    emCL := math.min(emCL, low)
// A late sample's crosses (the candle before, from the bar before) and this bar's own; with each,
// the day's number, the stay under the line, the flips before, and whether the filter calls it weak.
bool emLS = false
bool emLM = false
bool emLY = false
int  emLN = 0
int  emLU = 0
int  emLF = 0
bool emLW = false
bool emCS = false
bool emCM = false
bool emCY = false
int  emCN = 0
int  emCU = 0
int  emCF = 0
bool emCW = false
// v37: the same for the bounces — the lines that fired, the day's number, the stop (a tick under the
// pullback's low), the candles since the cross, what the pullback came down to, and weak or not.
bool  emBLS = false
bool  emBLM = false
bool  emBLY = false
int   emBLN = 0
float emBLStop = na
int   emBLAge = 0
bool  emBLE = false
bool  emBLV = false
bool  emBLW = false
bool  emBCS = false
bool  emBCM = false
bool  emBCY = false
int   emBCN = 0
float emBCStop = na
int   emBCAge = 0
bool  emBCE = false
bool  emBCV = false
bool  emBCW = false
if emOk
    if emLateS
        bool emOkL = inWindow and not newDay and (not emGainOn or gainer[1])
        // v37: an earlier cross's bounce first (a cross candle can't be its own bounce). Weak when none
        // of its lines' crosses was strong; only a strong bounce takes a day's number.
        bool emB1 = emBncOn and emSession and emS.stepBounce(emLive[1], svwap[1], emCOp, emCLp, close[1])
        bool emB2 = emBncOn and emMonth and emM.stepBounce(emLive[1], mvwap[1], emCOp, emCLp, close[1])
        bool emB3 = emBncOn and emYear and emY.stepBounce(emLive[1], yvwap[1], emCOp, emCLp, close[1])
        emBLS := emB1 and emOkL
        emBLM := emB2 and emOkL
        emBLY := emB3 and emOkL
        bool emH1 = emBLS and not emS.weakX
        bool emH2 = emBLM and not emM.weakX
        bool emH3 = emBLY and not emY.weakX
        emBLW := not (emH1 or emH2 or emH3)
        if emH1
            emS.bn := emS.bn + 1
        if emH2
            emM.bn := emM.bn + 1
        if emH3
            emY.bn := emY.bn + 1
        bool emQ1 = emBLW ? emBLS : emH1
        bool emQ2 = emBLW ? emBLM : emH2
        bool emQ3 = emBLW ? emBLY : emH3
        [emBLo1, emBAg1, emBE1, emBV1, emBN1] = emBRead(emS, emM, emY, emQ1, emQ2, emQ3)
        emBLStop := emBLo1 - syminfo.mintick
        emBLAge  := emBAg1
        emBLE    := emBE1
        emBLV    := emBV1
        emBLN    := emBN1
        bool emX1 = emSession and emS.crossUp(emHS, emLive[1], svwap[1])
        bool emX2 = emMonth and emM.crossUp(emHM, emLive[1], mvwap[1])
        bool emX3 = emYear and emY.crossUp(emHY, emLive[1], yvwap[1])
        emDone := emT[1]
        emLS := emX1 and emOkL
        emLM := emX2 and emOkL
        emLY := emX3 and emOkL
        // v36: the strong ones among them (the hour is the candle's own, by its open). Only a strong
        // cross takes a day's number, and a message is weak when none of its lines is strong.
        bool emEarlyL = hour(emT[1], "America/New_York") < emFromHour
        bool emG1 = emLS and not emWeak(emS, emEarlyL)
        bool emG2 = emLM and not emWeak(emM, emEarlyL)
        bool emG3 = emLY and not emWeak(emY, emEarlyL)
        emLW := not (emG1 or emG2 or emG3)
        if emG1
            emS.n := emS.n + 1
        if emG2
            emM.n := emM.n + 1
        if emG3
            emY.n := emY.n + 1
        // The message's numbers: the strong lines' when there is one, else the fired lines' (a weak
        // cross then carries the day's count so far, 0 before the first strong one).
        bool emP1 = emLW ? emLS : emG1
        bool emP2 = emLW ? emLM : emG2
        bool emP3 = emLW ? emLY : emG3
        emLN := emCount(emS, emM, emY, emP1, emP2, emP3)
        [emU1, emF1] = emRead(emS, emM, emY, emP1, emP2, emP3)
        emLU := emU1
        emLF := emF1
        // v37: a sent cross starts the wait for its bounce (weak if the cross was).
        if emLS
            emS.arm(not emG1)
        if emLM
            emM.arm(not emG2)
        if emLY
            emY.arm(not emG3)
    // The anchors: a new day restarts the session line and the day's counts, and ends every wait.
    if newDay
        emS.restart(emHS)
        emS.n := 0
        emM.n := 0
        emY.n := 0
        emS.bn := 0
        emM.bn := 0
        emY.bn := 0
        emM.armed := false
        emY.armed := false
    if emNewM
        emM.restart(emHM)
    if emNewY
        emY.restart(emHY)
    if emEnd and (na(emDone) or emDone != emT)
        bool emOkC = inWindow and (not emGainOn or gainer)
        bool emB4 = emBncOn and emSession and emS.stepBounce(emLive, svwap, emCO, emCL, close)
        bool emB5 = emBncOn and emMonth and emM.stepBounce(emLive, mvwap, emCO, emCL, close)
        bool emB6 = emBncOn and emYear and emY.stepBounce(emLive, yvwap, emCO, emCL, close)
        emBCS := emB4 and emOkC
        emBCM := emB5 and emOkC
        emBCY := emB6 and emOkC
        bool emH4 = emBCS and not emS.weakX
        bool emH5 = emBCM and not emM.weakX
        bool emH6 = emBCY and not emY.weakX
        emBCW := not (emH4 or emH5 or emH6)
        if emH4
            emS.bn := emS.bn + 1
        if emH5
            emM.bn := emM.bn + 1
        if emH6
            emY.bn := emY.bn + 1
        bool emQ4 = emBCW ? emBCS : emH4
        bool emQ5 = emBCW ? emBCM : emH5
        bool emQ6 = emBCW ? emBCY : emH6
        [emBLo2, emBAg2, emBE2, emBV2, emBN2] = emBRead(emS, emM, emY, emQ4, emQ5, emQ6)
        emBCStop := emBLo2 - syminfo.mintick
        emBCAge  := emBAg2
        emBCE    := emBE2
        emBCV    := emBV2
        emBCN    := emBN2
        bool emX4 = emSession and emS.crossUp(emHS, emLive, svwap)
        bool emX5 = emMonth and emM.crossUp(emHM, emLive, mvwap)
        bool emX6 = emYear and emY.crossUp(emHY, emLive, yvwap)
        emDone := emT
        emCS := emX4 and emOkC
        emCM := emX5 and emOkC
        emCY := emX6 and emOkC
        bool emEarlyC = hour(emT, "America/New_York") < emFromHour
        bool emG4 = emCS and not emWeak(emS, emEarlyC)
        bool emG5 = emCM and not emWeak(emM, emEarlyC)
        bool emG6 = emCY and not emWeak(emY, emEarlyC)
        emCW := not (emG4 or emG5 or emG6)
        if emG4
            emS.n := emS.n + 1
        if emG5
            emM.n := emM.n + 1
        if emG6
            emY.n := emY.n + 1
        bool emP4 = emCW ? emCS : emG4
        bool emP5 = emCW ? emCM : emG5
        bool emP6 = emCW ? emCY : emG6
        emCN := emCount(emS, emM, emY, emP4, emP5, emP6)
        [emU2, emF2] = emRead(emS, emM, emY, emP4, emP5, emP6)
        emCU := emU2
        emCF := emF2
        if emCS
            emS.arm(not emG4)
        if emCM
            emM.arm(not emG5)
        if emCY
            emY.arm(not emG6)

// The message — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage. Every value is the sampled
// candle's (a late one's from the bar before):
//   EMA OMH 8.09 | sVWAP 8.01 (+1.0%) | mVWAP 7.5 (+7.9%) | ema 9 8.03 | line session | candle 3 | cross 1 | under 12 | flips 1 | day high +25% | vwap 30s | tf 30S
// v36: `under N` = the candles the EMA had been at or under the line, `flips N` = its crossings of the
// line in the 20 candles before, and `| weak` after them when the filter calls the cross weak.
emPct(float px, float ln) => (px >= ln ? "+" : "") + str.tostring((px / ln - 1) * 100, "#.0")
emMsg(bool fS, bool fM, bool fY, int n, float px, float e, float sv, float mv, float yv, bool late, int under, int flips, bool weak) =>
    string names = ""
    if fS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
    if fM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
    if fY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
    string msg = "EMA " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(px, format.mintick)
    if not na(sv)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(sv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, sv) + "%)"
    if not na(mv)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, mv) + "%)"
    if not na(yv)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, yv) + "%)"
    msg += " | ema " + str.tostring(emLen) + " " + str.tostring(e, format.mintick)
    msg += " | line " + names + " | candle " + emTf + " | cross " + str.tostring(n)
    msg += " | under " + str.tostring(under) + " | flips " + str.tostring(flips)
    if weak
        msg += " | weak"
    if not na(dayHighGain)
        msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    if late
        msg += " | late"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period

// v37, the bounce's message (the same contract):
//   BOUNCE PARA 0.1021 | stop 0.0985 | sVWAP 0.0975 (+4.7%) | ema 9 0.099 | line session | from ema+vwap | candle 3 | bounce 1 | since 3 | day high +25% | vwap 30s | tf 30S
// `stop` = a tick under the pullback's low, `from` = what the pullback came down to (ema, vwap or
// ema+vwap), `since N` = candles after the cross candle, `| weak` when its cross was weak.
emBncMsg(bool fS, bool fM, bool fY, int n, float px, float e, float sv, float mv, float yv, bool late, float stop, int age, bool hitE, bool hitV, bool weak) =>
    string names = ""
    if fS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
    if fM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
    if fY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
    string msg = "BOUNCE " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(px, format.mintick) + " | stop " + str.tostring(stop, format.mintick)
    if not na(sv)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(sv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, sv) + "%)"
    if not na(mv)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, mv) + "%)"
    if not na(yv)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, yv) + "%)"
    msg += " | ema " + str.tostring(emLen) + " " + str.tostring(e, format.mintick)
    msg += " | line " + names + " | from " + (hitE and hitV ? "ema+vwap" : hitE ? "ema" : "vwap")
    msg += " | candle " + emTf + " | bounce " + str.tostring(n) + " | since " + str.tostring(age)
    if weak
        msg += " | weak"
    if not na(dayHighGain)
        msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    if late
        msg += " | late"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period

// From the 30s alert alone (the VB's alert timeframe), like the VB and the RSI.
if (emBLS or emBLM or emBLY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emBncMsg(emBLS, emBLM, emBLY, emBLN, close[1], emLive[1], svwap[1], mvwap[1], yvwap[1], true, emBLStop, emBLAge, emBLE, emBLV, emBLW), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if (emBCS or emBCM or emBCY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emBncMsg(emBCS, emBCM, emBCY, emBCN, close, emLive, svwap, mvwap, yvwap, false, emBCStop, emBCAge, emBCE, emBCV, emBCW), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if (emLS or emLM or emLY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emMsg(emLS, emLM, emLY, emLN, close[1], emLive[1], svwap[1], mvwap[1], yvwap[1], true, emLU, emLF, emLW), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if (emCS or emCM or emCY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emMsg(emCS, emCM, emCY, emCN, close, emLive, svwap, mvwap, yvwap, false, emCU, emCF, emCW), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
// v35 plots go last: the EMA line, the markers, and a VWAP line this setup uses that no other draws.
plot(emOk and emShow ? emLive : na, "EMA (EMA cross, v35)", color.aqua)
plotshape(emShow and (emCS or emCM or emCY) and not emCW, "EMA cross (v35)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.orange, text = "EMA", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
plotshape(emShow and (emLS or emLM or emLY) and not emLW, "EMA cross, late close (v35)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.orange, text = "EMA", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small, offset = -1)
plot(emOn and emSession and not ((pbOn and pbSession) or (vbOn and vbSession)) ? svwap : na, "sVWAP (EMA cross, v35)", color.purple)
plot(emOn and emMonth and not ((pbOn and pbMonth) or (vbOn and vbMonth)) ? mvwap : na, "mVWAP (EMA cross, v35)", color.yellow)
plot(emOn and emYear and not ((pbOn and pbYear) or (vbOn and vbYear)) ? yvwap : na, "yVWAP (EMA cross, v35)", color.blue)
// v36 plots go last: the crosses the filter calls weak, in gray (sent with `| weak`, stored, not announced).
plotshape(emShow and (emCS or emCM or emCY) and emCW, "EMA cross, filtered (v36)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "ema", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(emShow and (emLS or emLM or emLY) and emLW, "EMA cross, filtered, late close (v36)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "ema", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, offset = -1)
// v37 plots go last: the bounce after a cross (green), and the ones after a weak cross (gray).
plotshape(emShow and (emBCS or emBCM or emBCY) and not emBCW, "EMA bounce (v37)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.lime, text = "BNC", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
plotshape(emShow and (emBLS or emBLM or emBLY) and not emBLW, "EMA bounce, late close (v37)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.lime, text = "BNC", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small, offset = -1)
plotshape(emShow and (emBCS or emBCM or emBCY) and emBCW, "EMA bounce, filtered (v37)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "bnc", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(emShow and (emBLS or emBLM or emBLY) and emBLW, "EMA bounce, filtered, late close (v37)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "bnc", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, offset = -1)
